WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.050
Ms. Coffee Bean, what are you looking at?

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:08.860
Oh yeah, it is this new paper that took ViT,
scaled it up to 2 Billion parameters,

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:14.990
and ran it over 3 Billion images,
and casually set a new state-of-the-art on

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.020
ImageNet.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.080
Why did they do this?

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.130
Because they can.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.910
Because they Google.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.450
But now we know.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:27.170
Previously, there was always the question:
What would happen if we would go beyond the

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.600
300 Million images?

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:34.220
Well, this paper shows the scaling curve for
ViT up to the billions in terms of data and

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:35.290
parameters.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.960
Showing that… the more data the better.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.430
The more parameters, the better…

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:44.810
This scaling law for images, looks much like…
with GPT-3 for language.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.850
But now we know, Ms. Coffee Bean.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.149
Is your curiosity satisfied now?

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:50.460
Was it worth it?

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.460
[Sniff].

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.730
Ms. Coffee Bean, do you smell this?

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:56.179
Yeah, it smells like the best-paper award
for the next conference will ...

